# ARCHITAK Platform Rules

## Never

- Use `any` casually; prefer `unknown` and narrowing
- Commit secrets or put credentials in CMS / `site_settings`
- Expose `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, R2 secrets, or admin password to the browser
- Disable Supabase Row Level Security
- Ship a database table without RLS policies in the same migration
- Make the R2 bucket blindly public or serve `private/` via `media.architak.in`
- Convert entire pages to Client Components without need
- Load GSAP / Three.js globally
- Bypass admin authorization checks on the server

## Always

- Prefer Server Components; Client Components only for interaction
- Validate with Zod at UI and server boundaries
- Keep domain logic under `features/<domain>/`
- Use design tokens from `styles/tokens.css` (no arbitrary one-off spacing)
- Public pages must remain crawlable without client JS
- Authorize (static session or later Supabase Auth) **before** any service-role call
- Storage keys must start with `public/` or `private/` matching `visibility`
- Update docs when architecture decisions change
